LATEST IMPLEMENTATION — MB-02A
New types in mirror_core::v2: SignedTransferV2, TransferBodyV2, SignedOperationV2,
BlockHeaderV2, BlockV2 and operations_root_v2. Core now depends on personhood's
immutable config, typed membership operations and parent view. Personhood still
only depends on crypto. No dependency cycle or external package upgrade.

Transfer kind0 reuses the frozen 131-byte B2 prefix; recipient32, amount8, fee8,
signature64 make 243 signed bytes. Enroll/Approve/Withdraw remain 291/227/227 bytes.
V2 signing/ID domains unchanged; sender derives from actor using MIRROR_ADDRESS_V1.
Account sequence and membership sequence are separate. Sign/decode/from_parts are
not state authorization. Transfer validate_for_parent checks C, checked next height,
recent canonical anchor/window, positive amount, zero fee and strict signature.
It does not check balance, account nonce, member rights or mutate anything.
The old membership-only decoder and MPH2 still reject Transfer=0.

Header 160 bytes: versionu32=2, C32, heightu64, parent32, operations_root32,
ledger_root32, timestampu64, pow_bitsu32, nonceu64. Hash domain MIRROR_BLOCK_V2.
MRB2 is magic4 + header160 + countu32 + repeated(lengthu32, complete signed op);
empty168 bytes. Full ordered list retains transfer positions. Private immutable
fields prevent unchecked post-construction mutation.

Operation leaf H(MIRROR_OP_LEAF_V2 || u32lenLE || signed bytes). Existing Mirror
Merkle convention: H(empty), single leaf unchanged, odd last duplicated at each
level, pairs H(left||right). Final H(MIRROR_OP_ROOT_V2 || u32countLE || innerroot)
commits count and distinguishes duplicate-last ambiguity. H means SHA256d.
This root differs from legacy transaction roots and MPH2 group digests.

Decoder checks total bytes, counts, fixed lengths/kinds and member/enrollment
quotas in an allocation-free preflight before allocating the body vector. Direct
construction, encode, root and integrity paths also enforce config budgets.
BlockV2::verify_integrity checks budgets, header/operation C, operation root and
strict signatures. It DOES NOT check transfer policy/windows, balances/nonces,
actual ancestry/height/time/target/PoW, ledger root or genesis. Tests explicitly
show these limits. No accepted V2 block or mixed ledger exists yet.

tools/reference_blocks_v2.py independently computes 5 operation fixtures, 7 blocks,
9 header variants using the standard library. Five public test signatures were
separately generated/verified with Python cryptography. Rust independently signs
and reconstructs them; all 10 vector tests matched first run. No failed Rust result
became a fixture. block_v2_demo checks synthetic mixed bytes/context/integrity and
tamper rejection, while explicitly saying no balances/membership were executed and
claimed ledger root/PoW remain unvalidated.

